  <section>
    <templateId root="2.16.840.1.113883.10.20.22.2.9" extension="2014-06-09"/>
    <code code="51847-2" codeSystem="2.16.840.1.113883.6.1" displayName="Evaluation + Plan note"/>
    <title>Assessment and Plan</title>
    <text><list listType="ordered"><item><content styleCode="Bold">Amyotrophic lateral sclerosis, limb onset, with early bulbar signs (G12.21)</content>. ALSFRS-R 38, a fall of about one point a month since diagnosis. FVC 4.05 L (79%), maximal inspiratory pressure -70 cmH2O, no orthopnea: no criterion for ventilation yet. Weight 87.4 kg, 2.0% below diagnosis. New mild dysarthria and tongue fasciculations: early bulbar involvement. ALT 35 U/L at three months on riluzole. [S]<list><item>Continue riluzole; ALT every 3 months.</item><item>Speech therapy and voice banking; swallowing reviewed each visit.</item><item>Dietitian: an extra 500 kcal a day; gastrostomy information given.</item><item>Power wheelchair evaluation now, because of lead times.</item><item>Letter for workplace accommodations: accessible office, flexible hours, rest breaks, voice-recognition software, parking.</item></list></item><item><content styleCode="Bold">Left lateral ankle sprain (S93.402A)</content>. Resolved. [S]<list><item>Orthosis for all walking outdoors.</item></list></item></list><paragraph>Protocol monitoring: items the monitoring protocol calls for at this visit. [S]</paragraph><table><thead><tr><th>Domain</th><th>Measure</th><th>Interval</th><th>Status</th><th>Detail</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Survey</td><td>ALSFRS-R</td><td>Every 2 to 3 months in the multidisciplinary ALS clinic</td><td>Completed today</td><td>38 of 48</td></tr><tr><td>Imaging</td><td>Seated forced vital capacity</td><td>Every 2 to 3 months in the multidisciplinary ALS clinic</td><td>Completed today</td><td>4.05 L, 79% of predicted</td></tr><tr><td>Examination</td><td>Maximal inspiratory pressure; supine capacity and overnight oximetry when values fall or symptoms appear</td><td>Every 2 to 3 months in the multidisciplinary ALS clinic</td><td>Completed today</td><td>Maximal inspiratory pressure -70 cmH2O; no orthopnea; supine test not yet needed</td></tr><tr><td>Examination</td><td>Noninvasive ventilation criteria (FVC below 50%, maximal inspiratory pressure weaker than -60 cmH2O, nocturnal desaturation, orthopnea)</td><td>Every 2 to 3 months in the multidisciplinary ALS clinic</td><td>Not indicated</td><td>No criterion met</td></tr><tr><td>Examination</td><td>Weight and BMI (gastrostomy discussion if weight falls 5 to 10% or swallowing is unsafe; place while FVC is above 50%)</td><td>Every visit</td><td>Completed today</td><td>87.4 kg, 2.0% below diagnosis; extra calories advised</td></tr><tr><td>Examination</td><td>Speech and swallowing assessment</td><td>Every 2 to 3 months in the multidisciplinary ALS clinic</td><td>Completed today</td><td>Mild dysarthria; swallowing normal; voice banking started</td></tr><tr><td>Survey</td><td>Cognitive and behavioral screening</td><td>At diagnosis and periodically</td><td>Up to date</td><td>Normal at diagnosis; no change reported</td></tr><tr><td>Survey</td><td>Depression (PHQ-9)</td><td>Every visit</td><td>Completed today</td><td>PHQ-9 7</td></tr><tr><td>Examination</td><td>Symptoms: cramps, spasticity, saliva, emotional lability, pain</td><td>Every visit</td><td>Completed today</td><td>Cramps controlled with stretching; no drooling or emotional lability</td></tr><tr><td>Examination</td><td>Mobility, falls, orthoses and equipment</td><td>Every visit</td><td>Completed today</td><td>Orthosis and cane; no falls since the sprain; power wheelchair evaluation ordered</td></tr><tr><td>Laboratory</td><td>ALT on riluzole</td><td>Monthly for 3 months, then every 3 months</td><td>Completed today</td><td>ALT 35 U/L at three months; 41 U/L at two months (sick visit); next in 3 months</td></tr><tr><td>Referral</td><td>Multidisciplinary ALS clinic</td><td>Every 2 to 3 months in the multidisciplinary ALS clinic</td><td>Completed today</td><td>Seen today</td></tr><tr><td>Self-management</td><td>Work, disability benefits and social work</td><td>From diagnosis</td><td>Completed today</td><td>Accommodation letter written for a desk role</td></tr><tr><td>Self-management</td><td>Advance care planning</td><td>Early, then at each change</td><td>Due</td><td>At the preventive visit next month</td></tr></tbody></table><paragraph>Goal progress:</paragraph><list><item>A clear diagnosis, with mimics excluded, within four weeks. Outcome by 2026-05-18: Diagnosis made at two weeks on EMG, MRI and blood tests [S]</item><item>No falls, using an ankle-foot orthosis, a cane, and a safer home. In progress; target 2026-10-19 [S]</item><item>Weight held within 5% of the weight at diagnosis. In progress; target 2026-10-19 [S]</item><item>Breathing tracked every visit, with noninvasive ventilation started as soon as criteria are met. In progress; target 2026-10-19 [S]</item><item>Goals of care, a health care agent, and his wishes about ventilation and feeding recorded early and revisited. In progress; target 2026-09-21 [S]</item><item>Working in a role that suits him, with accommodations. In progress; target 2026-10-19 [S]</item></list><paragraph>Guideline basis: Practice parameter update: the care of the patient with amyotrophic lateral sclerosis: drug, nutritional, and respiratory therapies (an evidence-based review) (2009); Practice parameter update: the care of the patient with amyotrophic lateral sclerosis: multidisciplinary care, symptom management, and cognitive/behavioral impairment (an evidence-based review) (2009); The ALSFRS-R: a revised ALS functional rating scale that incorporates assessments of respiratory function (1999)</paragraph><paragraph>Follow-up: Preventive visit in four weeks. ALS clinic in about eight weeks with breathing tests. Next scheduled visit 2026-09-21: periodic adult preventive visit. [S]</paragraph></text>

